<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="/static/theatlantic/syndication/feeds/atom-to-html.e8fb83e50eaf.xsl" ?><feed xml:lang="en-us" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><title>Technology | The Atlantic</title><link href="https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/" rel="alternate"></link><link href="https://www.theatlantic.com/feed/channel/technology/" rel="self"></link><id>https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/</id><updated>2026-11-25T15:31:27-05:00</updated><rights>Copyright 2026 by The Atlantic Monthly Group. All Rights Reserved.</rights><entry><id>tag:theatlantic.com,2026:50-689587</id><author><name>Victoria Feng</name><uri>http://www.theatlantic.com/author/victoria-feng/?utm_source=feed</uri></author><media:content url="https://cdn.theatlantic.com/thumbor/Fr_PLjmw4X5d_HyrgsKi9J-TCZo=/media/img/mt/2026/11/2026_11_16_ThePeopleWhoAreOutsourcingHolidayShopping/original.jpg"><media:credit>Illustration by Liz Hart / The Atlantic. Source: Getty.</media:credit></media:content><title type="html">Here Comes Santa Claude</title><published>2026-11-25T13:17:00-05:00</published><updated>2026-11-25T15:31:27-05:00</updated><summary type="html">Some Americans are about to open holiday gifts that were chosen and purchased entirely by AI agents.</summary><link href="https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/2026/11/ai-agents-holiday-shopping-muse/689587/?utm_source=feed" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link></entry><entry><id>tag:theatlantic.com,2026:50-689552</id><author><name>Charlie Warzel</name><uri>http://www.theatlantic.com/author/charlie-warzel/?utm_source=feed</uri></author><media:content url="https://cdn.theatlantic.com/thumbor/SGevK25weZlSrZNoVG_MDoKtglA=/media/img/mt/2026/11/2026_11_23_Silicon_Valley_Holding_Economy_Hostage/original.jpg"><media:credit>David Paul Morris / Bloomberg / Getty</media:credit></media:content><title type="html">The Economy Is a Hostage Situation</title><published>2026-11-23T15:30:51-05:00</published><updated>2026-11-23T16:36:24-05:00</updated><summary type="html">America has two choices under Nvidia’s market dominance, and both are bad.</summary><link href="https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/2026/11/ai-hostage-economy-nvidia-huang/689552/?utm_source=feed" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link></entry><entry><id>tag:theatlantic.com,2026:50-689549</id><author><name>Matteo Wong</name><uri>http://www.theatlantic.com/author/matteo-wong/?utm_source=feed</uri></author><media:content url="https://cdn.theatlantic.com/thumbor/mtH8VoKyYzk01Diac9zZbWuqVwE=/media/img/mt/2026/11/2026_11_23_shameless_valley_/original.jpg"><media:credit>Jonathan Ernst / Reuters</media:credit></media:content><title type="html">A Shameless Valley</title><published>2026-11-23T14:48:24-05:00</published><updated>2026-11-23T16:24:10-05:00</updated><summary type="html">The time it apparently takes to atone for your sins in Silicon Valley: less than two weeks.</summary><link href="https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/2026/11/silicon-valley-shameless-nvidia/689549/?utm_source=feed" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link></entry><entry><id>tag:theatlantic.com,2026:50-689517</id><author><name>Will Oremus</name><uri>http://www.theatlantic.com/author/will-oremus/?utm_source=feed</uri></author><media:content url="https://cdn.theatlantic.com/thumbor/OuHT5pRcV2SCPS2UEEAiTmcFN_s=/media/img/mt/2026/11/2026_11_19_Elon_Musks_MAGA_Pivot_2198394195/original.jpg"><media:credit>Jim Watson / AFP / Getty</media:credit></media:content><title type="html">‘I’m Not MAGA,’ Says Man in MAGA Hat</title><published>2026-11-19T19:51:00-05:00</published><updated>2026-11-20T12:27:52-05:00</updated><summary type="html">Elon Musk would like to pretend that the past two years didn’t happen.</summary><link href="https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/2026/11/elon-musk-maga-pivot/689517/?utm_source=feed" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link></entry><entry><id>tag:theatlantic.com,2026:50-689505</id><author><name>Charlie Warzel</name><uri>http://www.theatlantic.com/author/charlie-warzel/?utm_source=feed</uri></author><media:content url="https://cdn.theatlantic.com/thumbor/1_S7LQeEzKIPYgFSmey9C_N6RN0=/media/img/mt/2026/11/2026_11_18_Model_collapse/original.gif"><media:credit>Illustration by The Atlantic</media:credit></media:content><title type="html">Silicon Valley Is Suffering From Model Collapse</title><published>2026-11-19T16:46:56-05:00</published><updated>2026-11-23T13:19:51-05:00</updated><summary type="html">Why do tech leaders sound so illogical and off-putting?</summary><link href="https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/2026/11/silicon-valley-model-collapse/689505/?utm_source=feed" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link></entry></feed>